course: religion-ethics
lesson: 53
title: Why living things die, and the circle of life in nature
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Every living thing, a sunflower, a bee, a fox or a person, has a body that wears out or gets badly hurt or ill in the end; when the body stops working completely, the heart stops, breathing stops and the brain stops, and it does not start again.
explain: Dead is not asleep: a sleeping cat still breathes and will wake up, but a dead bee on the windowsill will never move again, however gently Jayden pokes it.
explain: In autumn Josh kicks through dead brown leaves, but the tree is alive and resting; the leaves rot with worms, fungi and bacteria into rich soil that feeds next spring's growth, just as the compost heap turns old peel into food for new plants.
explain: So the food chain is really a circle: the sun feeds the grass, the grass feeds the rabbit, the rabbit feeds the fox, and when the fox dies, beetles, worms and bacteria turn it back into soil for the grass.
explain: Why we must die at all is one of the biggest questions there is: Christians believe death is not the end because Jesus rose from the dead, other faiths have their own answers, many non-religious people say death is simply part of nature, and grown-ups do not have all the answers.
fact: When a living thing dies, its body stops working completely and will not start again.
fact: Death is not sleep: a sleeping animal still breathes and has a heartbeat, and it will wake.
fact: Many trees drop their leaves in autumn and rest through winter; the leaves die, but the tree lives on.
fact: Worms, fungi and bacteria break down dead plants and animals into soil; this is called decomposition.
fact: A food chain shows who eats whom, starting from the sun and plants; when animals die, decomposers return them to the soil, so the chain is really a circle.
fact: Lions are meat-eaters and cannot live on grass; hunting is how they feed themselves and their cubs, not cruelty.
fact: Sunflowers live for one summer: they grow, flower, make seeds and die, which is their natural life.
fact: Some living things die young through illness, accidents or bad conditions; often nobody can know the exact reason.
fact: Most meat comes from farm animals; some people, vegetarians and vegans, choose not to eat meat, and many Hindus and Buddhists are vegetarian because their faiths teach care for animal life.
fact: Dinosaurs (apart from the ones that became birds) died out about 66 million years ago; there is no sign that people will die out any time soon, and many people work hard to keep the Earth safe.
fact: At burials Christians say «earth to earth, ashes to ashes, dust to dust», remembering that bodies return to the earth, with the hope of resurrection.
fact: Jesus said not one sparrow falls without God knowing, and that a seed must fall into the ground and die to make many seeds.
exercise: Josh kicks through brown leaves in autumn. Is the tree dying? | No, the leaves are dead but the tree is resting until spring | Yes, a whole tree dies every autumn and a brand new one grows | Yes, kicking the leaves is what kills the tree | No, the leaves are only asleep and will jump back on
exercise: Ava's compost heap is full of rotting peel and worms. Why keep it? | Worms and bacteria turn it into soil that feeds new plants | It keeps rats away from the house | Rotting food slowly turns into brand new fruit all by itself | It is where the bin men collect rubbish
exercise: Ethan sees a lion catch a zebra and calls it mean. What is true? | Lions eat meat to feed themselves and their cubs, not to be cruel | Lions kill only because they really enjoy being cruel to other animals | Lions could eat grass if they tried harder | Zebras let themselves be caught to help lions
exercise: Mila asks why everyone has to die. What is the most honest answer? | Every body wears out in the end; faiths give different hopes about what follows | Only people who are bad have to die | Scientists have found a cure, but keep it secret | People die because they stop believing in God
exercise: Jayden pokes a bee and it does not move. How can you tell dead from asleep? | Dead means no breathing or heartbeat, and it will never wake | Asleep and dead are really the same thing when it comes to insects | A dead bee is just sleeping very deeply | A dead creature always feels warm and soft
exercise: Leah's sunflower has gone brown and droopy. Did she kill it? | No, sunflowers live one summer, flower, make seeds and die | Yes, she watered it too much every day | Yes, sunflowers live for ever and ever unless someone harms them | No, it is only pretending, to rest for a week
exercise: The class poster shows sun, grass, rabbit, fox. What eats the fox in the end? | When it dies, beetles, worms and bacteria turn it into soil | Nothing, foxes never die | The rabbit, once it grows bigger | The sun, which burns it up
exercise: Ollie's goldfish died but his friend's is five years old. Why do some die young? | Illness, accidents or bad conditions, and often nobody knows | Young deaths happen only to fish that have been bad or naughty | Goldfish live exactly one year, no more and no less, every time | Fish always die young when their owners are sad or grumpy at home
exercise: Isla learns farm animals become food and says she won't eat lamb. What is true? | Some people eat meat and some choose not to; both are allowed | Everyone must eat meat to stay alive | Eating meat is against every religion | Refusing meat is rude to the cook and must always be punished at once
exercise: Freddie's mum says Grandad's body «stopped working». What does that mean? | His heart, breathing and brain stopped, and they cannot start again | He went into a very deep sleep for a while | His body is broken, but a mechanic or a doctor can mend it like new | He is on holiday and will come back later
exercise: Hannah hears dinosaurs died out. Will people die out soon too? | There is no sign of it; people work hard to keep the Earth safe | Yes, scientists say it will happen next year, or the year after | Yes, because people are related to dinosaurs | No, because people can never die at all
exercise: What do Christians say at burials about bodies returning to the earth? | Earth to earth, ashes to ashes, dust to dust | Sleep well now, and wake up again tomorrow morning | Gone today, but back again home by next Sunday | Dust to gold, and gold to dust, for ever and ever
exercise: What did Jesus say about sparrows? | Not one falls without God knowing | Sparrows are not worth caring about | Only sparrows go to heaven | Sparrows never die at all
exercise: Why are many Hindus and Buddhists vegetarian? | Their faith teaches care for animal life | Meat is forbidden by law in all their countries | They cannot digest meat at all | Their religions say vegetables are holy gods
exercise: What does the word «decomposition» mean? | Dead things being broken down into soil by small living things | A kind of music played at funerals | The way bones turn into stone overnight | Fresh food being kept cold in a fridge
test: A Gen Alpha kid shouts, «that dead bee is just sleeping, no cap, it'll get up, skibidi!» («No cap» means «no lie»; «skibidi» means nothing at all.) What is true? | A dead bee will never wake; death is not sleep | Bees sleep standing perfectly still for a whole week | It will wake up again if someone sings a song to it | Dead insects always come back to life every spring
test: Your nan in Yorkshire mutters, «Them leaves are all dead, love, but t'tree's champion.» («Champion» means «fine, doing well».) What does she mean? | The leaves have died, but the tree is alive and resting | The tree has won a prize in a competition for the best tree | The tree will die completely before the winter comes in | The leaves will all turn green again on the tree next week
test: What would happen if nothing in nature ever rotted? | Dead plants and animals would pile up and the soil would not be fed | Nothing would change at all | Plants would grow faster without soil | Animals would never need to eat again
test: Your brother says, «Lions are evil, they murder zebras.» Which reply is best? | Lions hunt to eat; feeling sad for the zebra is fine, but lions are not cruel on purpose | He is right, lions should be locked up for ever | He is right, lions kill for fun only | Zebras deserve it for being slow
test: Leah sobs, «I proper killed it!» about her drooping sunflower. What is the kind, true answer? | No, sunflowers live one summer; save the seeds for spring | Yes, you should never grow flowers again | Yes, flowers only ever die when people are careless with them | It is not dead, just shy of autumn
test: A cartoon shows a fox in a food chain that lives for ever because nothing eats it. What does it get wrong? | Every fox dies, and decomposers return it to the soil | Foxes really do live for ever out in the wild, if left alone | Foxes eat the sun itself in the end, at the top of the chain | Food chains always end with a dragon or some other monster
test: An Aussie mate says, «Yeah nah, if dinos carked it, we're all next, heaps soon.» («Carked it» means «died».) What is the calm, true answer? | Many kinds have died out, but there is no sign people will soon | He is right, it will happen within weeks | Dinosaurs never really died out | People are bigger than dinosaurs, so it is impossible for us to die out
test: Isla's cousin teases, «You don't eat lamb? That's well peng... NOT.» («Peng» means «great», said sarcastically.) What is the fair view? | Eating meat or not is a choice; respect people who choose differently | Not eating lamb is silly and childish | Everybody who eats any meat is cruel and should be ashamed of themselves | Only grown-ups may choose what they eat
test: Freddie asks, «So Grandad just stopped, like a car?» Which answer is most honest? | In a way: the heart and breathing stopped, and they cannot start again | Yes, and he can be jump-started like a car | No, he only paused and will start again | No, people never really stop
test: Mila asks the vicar, «Why can't God just make us live for ever here?» What would the vicar most likely say? | Christians believe death is not the end, because Jesus rose again | God has forgotten about the people who die | Everyone lives for ever on earth if they pray hard enough every day | Only vicars get to live for ever
test: Ollie's mum says, «We don't know why your fish died, love.» Why is that an honest answer? | Often nobody can know the exact reason a creature dies young | She knows the real reason, but wants to keep it a secret from him | She is quite sure it was Ollie's fault, but is too kind to say | Fish deaths are never real deaths, so there is nothing to know
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the condition of death in a living organism? | The complete and irreversible cessation of bodily functions | A temporary condition analogous to sleep | A state from which the organism will awaken in due course | A condition confined to organisms of advanced age and great infirmity
exam: Identify the principal function of decomposers within an ecosystem. | The conversion of dead organic matter into soil nutrients | The hunting and killing of large mammals for food by night | The production of light for the growth of plants in the shade | The prevention of all decay in nature so that nothing rots
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning the annual sunflower. | It completes its natural life cycle within a single growing season | It persists indefinitely unless damaged or neglected by its owner | It dies solely in consequence of excessive watering | It hibernates throughout the winter and flowers again
exam: Ascertain the reason for which the lion kills other animals. | It is carnivorous and requires meat for its sustenance and that of its young | It derives entertainment from the suffering of its prey | It is incapable of distinguishing prey from companions | It is commanded to do so by its keepers
